# Distributed LLM Training on 3 Nodes (Kathara)

## 1. Dataset Preparation (on Host PC)

Convert raw text into the JSONL format required by the model:

py converter_dataset.py

This reads raw text (e.g., input.txt or wiki_it.txt), slices it into chunks of 400 characters, and creates pretrain_data.jsonl.

---

## 2. Train the BPE Tokenizer (on Host PC)

Train the custom tokenizer with a vocabulary size of 6400:

py train_tokenizer.py --dataset_path pretrain_data.jsonl --output_dir custom_tokenizer --vocab_size 6400 --evaluate

Check that evaluation prints: "Decoded text matches original: True".

---

## 3. Copy Files to Shared Storage

Copy dataset and tokenizer into the lab shared directory:

mkdir shared\train-tiny-llm
copy pretrain_data.jsonl shared\train-tiny-llm\
xcopy /E /I custom_tokenizer shared\train-tiny-llm\custom_tokenizer
copy pretrain_distributed.py shared\train-tiny-llm\
xcopy /E /I transformer shared\train-tiny-llm\transformer

---

## 4. Start the Lab Environment

From the lab folder containing lab.conf (cmd):

kathara lstart

Attach Wireshark to collision domain A:

kathara lconfig -n wireshark --add A

Open browser at:
http://localhost:3000

---

## 5. Launch Distributed Training (3 Nodes)

The script accepts parameters: <RANK> <SYNC_EVERY> <WORLD_SIZE>.

On pc1 (Rank 0 - Master):
python3 /shared/train-tiny-llm/pretrain_distributed.py 0 10 3

Immediately after, on pc2 (Rank 1):
python3 /shared/train-tiny-llm/pretrain_distributed.py 1 10 3

Immediately after, on pc3 (Rank 2):
python3 /shared/train-tiny-llm/pretrain_distributed.py 2 10 3

---

## 6. Test Model via Web App (on Host PC)

Copy the saved checkpoint back to your local repo (or point web_app.py to the shared folder) and run Streamlit:

py -m streamlit run web_app.py

Open browser at http://localhost:8501 to test text generation interactively.

---

## 7. Stop the Lab

When finished, shut down nodes from the host terminal:

kathara lclean
